**Hypothesis:**  
When a cannon is moved from one column to another, it keeps whatever damage it has accumulated from previous merges; the damage does **not** reset to the base value of 1.

```json
{
  "predicted_outcome": "winnable",
  "levelNumber": 1,
  "password": "Z0001",
  "isHard": false,
  "filas": [
    { "cuadros": [] },
    { "cuadros": [] },
    { "cuadros": [] },
    { "cuadros": [] },
    { "cuadros": [] },
    {
      "cuadros": [
        { "index": 1, "tipo": 4, "hp": 5 }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

When a cannon is placed onto a column that already contains a cannon (i.e., merges), and that column also contains a pirate, the merged cannon does **not** fire at the pirate during that same round; the pirate can only be hit starting the next round.

```json
{
  "predicted_outcome": "unwinnable",
  "levelNumber": 1,
  "password": "A0001",
  "isHard": false,
  "filas": [
    {
      "cuadros": [
        {"index": 0, "tipo": 1, "hp": 2}
      ]
    },
    {
      "cuadros": []
    },
    {
      "cuadros": [
        {"index": 4, "tipo": 4, "hp": 1}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

If two pirates appear in the same wave in different columns, each with HP ≤ 3, the level is unwinnable because only one cannon can be placed (or moved/merged) per round, so both pirates will inevitably reach position 3 before both can be killed, even when using merges.

```json
{
  "predicted_outcome": "unwinnable",
  "levelNumber": 1,
  "password": "A0001",
  "isHard": false,
  "filas": [
    {
      "cuadros": [
        { "index": 0, "tipo": 1, "hp": 3 },
        { "index": 1, "tipo": 4, "hp": 3 }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

**Hypothesis:**  
When a cannon is placed onto a column that already contains a cannon **and** a pirate, the merge (damage addition) happens before the shoot phase, and the resulting higher‑damage cannon fires at the pirate in that same round.

